{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"PyTorch’s ROCm `linspace` has a fused division/multiplication rounding pattern that is not reproduced by algebraically equivalent Triton expressions—several coordinates differ by one ULP, which then contaminates whole embedding rows. I’m temporarily sourcing only the small coordinate tables from PyTorch’s exact `linspace` implementation; this isolates the remaining bilinear arithmetic while preserving the fused bulk kernel."}}
